# Life Command OS — .gitignore
#
# PRIV-001: real personal data must never enter tracked content or Git history.
# PRIV-002: development and automated tests use neutral synthetic data only.
#
# This file is defence in depth, not the strategy. The strategy is ADR-0007:
# the repository contains synthetic data only, permanently. Never use `git add -f`
# to bypass these rules.

# --- Private runtime data and exports (PRIV-001, PRIV-003) ---
# Real life data lives in local IndexedDB and must never be committed.
*.backup
*.lcos-backup
/exports/
/backups/
/local-data/
/private/
/owner-only/
*.indexeddb
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# --- Owner-only and private capture ---
/screenshots/private/
/docs/private/
*.private.*
*.owner.*

# --- Secrets and environment ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets.json
credentials.json

# --- Dependencies and build output ---
#
# Build and test-output rules are anchored with a leading slash so they match only
# the directory at the repository root. An unanchored `coverage/` matches a directory
# of that name at ANY depth, and in Phase 8 it silently swallowed
# `src/command-core/coverage/` — three source files that `git add -A` reported adding,
# that `git status` hid behind their parent directory, and whose absence only appeared
# as a type-resolution failure in CI. Anchor anything that names a build artifact.
#
# `node_modules/` stays unanchored deliberately: a nested one should always be ignored.
node_modules/
/dist/
# The end-to-end build. Identical to production except that it includes the test
# bridge, which is why it is built separately and never deployed.
/dist-e2e/
/dist-ssr/
/build/
*.local

# --- Test and tooling output ---
/coverage/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/playwright/.cache/
/blob-report/
/.vitest/

# --- Editor and OS ---
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo

# --- Logs ---
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
